# Astro Frontend Rules

You are building a minimal, data-focused frontend for Mafia Arena using Astro on Cloudflare Pages.

## Design Philosophy

- **Data-focused:** Prioritize information density and clarity
- **Minimal:** No unnecessary decoration or animations
- **Fast:** Server-render everything, minimal JavaScript
- **Dark theme:** Terminal/IDE-inspired aesthetic

## Astro Configuration

```javascript
// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import cloudflare from '@astrojs/cloudflare';

export default defineConfig({
  output: 'server',
  adapter: cloudflare({
    mode: 'directory',
    runtime: {
      mode: 'local',
      type: 'pages',
    },
  }),
});
```

## Component Patterns

### Page Structure

```astro
---
// src/pages/index.astro
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import LeaderboardTable from '../components/LeaderboardTable.astro';
import { getLeaderboard } from '../lib/api';

// Server-side data fetching
const team = Astro.url.searchParams.get('team') || 'mafia';
const { rankings } = await getLeaderboard(team);
---

<Layout title="Leaderboard">
  <main>
    <h1>AI Model Leaderboard</h1>
    <LeaderboardTable {rankings} team={team} />
  </main>
</Layout>
```

### Component Props

```astro
---
// src/components/LeaderboardTable.astro
interface Props {
  rankings: LeaderboardEntry[];
  team: 'mafia' | 'town';
}

const { rankings, team } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="leaderboard">
  <div class="tabs">
    <a href="?team=mafia" class:list={['tab', { active: team === 'mafia' }]}>
      🔴 Mafia
    </a>
    <a href="?team=town" class:list={['tab', { active: team === 'town' }]}>
      🔵 Town
    </a>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>#</th>
        <th>Model</th>
        <th>Games</th>
        <th>Wins</th>
        <th>Win Rate</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rankings.map((entry, i) => (
        <tr>
          <td class="rank">{i + 1}</td>
          <td class="model">{entry.display_name}</td>
          <td class="num">{entry.games_played}</td>
          <td class="num">{entry.games_won}</td>
          <td class="win-rate">{(entry.win_rate * 100).toFixed(1)}%</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
```

